// Exercises the SDF transform helpers: map the world point into a shape's
// local frame with the homogeneous-affine inverse, evaluate the shape there
// with remap, and correct the distance by the conservative Lipschitz factor.

// A unit sphere centered at the origin, evaluated at the global point p.
unitSphere() {
  return length(p) - 1;
}

// World transform: scale up 2x, then translate. Non-uniform-safe path uses
// the smallest axis scale as the conservative factor.
xf = matrix.multiply(matrix.translation([3, 0, 0]), matrix.scaling([2, 2, 2]));
inv = matrix.inverse(xf);

// Sample point mapped into local space, and a transformed ray direction.
local = vector.multiplyPoint(inv, p);
dir = vector.multiplyVector(xf, [0, 0, 1]);

// Transformed SDF with the Lipschitz distance correction.
d = remap(unitSphere(), local) * matrix.minScale(xf);

return d + dir[0] * 0;
